              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FizzyZest5283"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Ok, I have not made this exact recipe but I grew up with something very similar that my mother made. It's pretty darn close to my mother's recipe; some of the amounts are different but the biggest difference is that my mother's does not include vanilla (it calls for 1.5 tbsp lemon juice) and uses flour instead of cornstarch. She initially made a pie but eventually skipped the crust and just made cheese custard instead. We loved it. Oh and we often made it with cottage cheese instead of ricotta.",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-13T21:20:46.125Z"
          },
